{"kind": "hair", "attachment": null, "findings": [{"level": "error", "title": "2 voxels are almost black", "body": "Trove's style guide asks for nothing darker than (10, 10, 10) - pure black reads as a hole in game. Use a dark grey instead.", "voxels": [4, 5]}, {"level": "warning", "title": "2 voxels are not connected to the model", "body": "These only touch the rest of the model at a corner, or not at all. Trove renders them, but the style guide asks for face-connected geometry.", "voxels": [3, 5]}, {"level": "warning", "title": "This model stores no attachment point", "body": "Older blueprints (format v3/v4) don't record an origin, so there's nothing to check and nothing to show. The game positions these by other means.", "voxels": []}], "satisfied": ["A blueprint stores one material per voxel, so alpha-on-solid and specular-on-glass - two of the classic .qb mistakes - can't happen here."], "counts": {"error": 1, "warning": 2, "info": 0}}